WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.247 --> 00:00:03.425
- [Tiffany] This is my friend
Laura, and she's 80 years old.

00:00:03.425 --> 00:00:07.592
- [Laura] And this is my
friend Tiffany, and she is 26.

00:00:08.899 --> 00:00:13.066
- [Tiffany] And we live
in a retirement community.

00:00:14.706 --> 00:00:18.172
(upbeat violin music)

00:00:18.172 --> 00:00:20.166
I'm a part of of the
Artist-in-Residence program

00:00:20.166 --> 00:00:21.617
at Judson Manor,

00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:23.683
which is a residential program where

00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:26.722
young musicians get to live here rent-free

00:00:26.722 --> 00:00:30.889
in exchange for performing
recitals and concerts.

00:00:30.889 --> 00:00:33.863
When I tell people I live
in a retirement community,

00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:35.838
I get a lot of mixed reactions.

00:00:35.838 --> 00:00:37.978
Some people don't believe me,

00:00:37.978 --> 00:00:41.395
other people think it's a wonderful idea.

00:00:42.321 --> 00:00:46.488
- I had not been a part of
this community more than

00:00:47.416 --> 00:00:49.033
two days

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:52.033
I was in the lobby and
they told me about Tiffany,

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.624
and I walked over and introduced myself,

00:00:54.624 --> 00:00:57.572
and I said, "Do you like dogs?"

00:00:57.572 --> 00:00:59.940
Oh, she loves dogs.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.394
And Tiffany and I became friends,

00:01:02.394 --> 00:01:05.228
we just formed a friendship.

00:01:05.228 --> 00:01:09.047
We'll talk about art,
we talk about clothes.

00:01:09.047 --> 00:01:11.687
I don't wear fashionable shoes anymore,

00:01:11.687 --> 00:01:15.187
but Tiffany does, and we talk about shoes.

00:01:17.302 --> 00:01:20.762
- Laura, to me, is like a grandma,

00:01:20.762 --> 00:01:24.032
and also a friend, and a confidante.

00:01:24.032 --> 00:01:26.604
I don't think the age difference is

00:01:26.604 --> 00:01:28.738
something that I am
constantly thinking about,

00:01:28.738 --> 00:01:30.135
or that I'm aware of.

00:01:30.135 --> 00:01:32.563
You don't think, oh,
I'm having dinner with

00:01:32.563 --> 00:01:36.212
this 100-year-old and this 90-year old,

00:01:36.212 --> 00:01:40.295
I'm having dinner with my
friend Laura and Sarah.

00:01:41.211 --> 00:01:45.490
In a way it is almost like
being in a college dorm

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:47.662
with the fact that there
are so many people here

00:01:47.662 --> 00:01:51.356
from different places,
from different backgrounds.

00:01:51.356 --> 00:01:53.576
It might be a little bit quieter

00:01:53.576 --> 00:01:56.148
than a normal college dorm,

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:59.127
but I think we still
have just as much fun.

00:01:59.127 --> 00:02:02.210
(gentle piano music)

